1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:04,480
I had already told you about Sandrine Ruffli and Léa as well.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
They are the ones who made these books.

3
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,640
They identified the houses that dated from the 15th century on the map.

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:15,980
I am right here.

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:20,640
Here, I rediscovered a little of the life of the house.

6
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:24,420
We had owned this house since around the 1960s.

7
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,780
My parents lived near Madrid, in Guadalajara.

8
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,660
And I had family here.

9
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:33,020
So they were tenants,

10
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,620
and my father worked for the brickworks.

11
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:36,960
I studied for a while,

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,980
then I managed as best I could,

13
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,900
and it was my parents who lived here

14
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,060
until they passed away.

15
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,200
So I retired in 2015.

16
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:46,900
I came here,

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,700
knowing that I owned two properties and wanting to restore them.

18
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:50,940
So, well,

19
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:53,080
this house has a soul.

20
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,520
I slept in this room.

21
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,180
So here, do you see this wall?

22
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:04,920
There used to be a corridor here.

23
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:07,600
It extended up to here.

24
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:10,120
There was a small door here.

25
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:12,180
You entered the kitchen, which was over there.

26
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:14,100
And here there was a rice boiler.

27
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,440
So I said, that's a lot of rooms.

28
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,460
We knocked everything down.

29
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:22,360
And we said, afterward we'll see what we find.

30
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:26,420
The first thing we found that really excited me was this wall.

31
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:27,700
Then the beams.

32
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:30,600
And I said, now let's see what the ceiling looks like.

33
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,040
So I spoke with Aquilino.

34
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:37,280
He told me, if I were you, I'd have the beams sandblasted and leave them as they are.

35
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:41,600
Little by little, we tried to modernize the house

36
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,420
while respecting its history.

37
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:50,640
This house had previously been restored by my parents as best they could.

38
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,520
And more poorly than well, to be honest.

39
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:53,700
But they only had the means they had.

40
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,460
There was thick vinyl wallpaper everywhere.

41
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,540
So I told the colleague I was working with,

42
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,460
let's strip everything away, and as we went upward,

43
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:03,360
while I was away working,

44
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:06,060
he called me and said, I think there's a painting underneath.

45
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,600
You'll see — we can go upstairs if you'd like.

46
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,820
Normally, the light comes on automatically.

47
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,120
There we go, by itself.

48
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,020
We arrive upstairs, and this is the painting.

49
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:35,760
When he talks about the spinner, I don't know if you can see it, but there is a spinning wheel and the thread running to her hand.

50
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:43,180
And when we removed the covering, as you can see there wasn't much there — you're looking directly at the wattle-and-daub; the plaster was only about 3 mm thick.

51
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,520
And then there was yet another layer on top.

52
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,240
That helped preserve the painting.

53
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:51,280
Perhaps one day I'll have it restored, we'll see.

54
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:55,720
I knew my parents' way of life,

55
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:57,160
as Coluche used to say,

56
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,560
the end of the month came on the 20th or even the 10th.

57
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,400
So today,

58
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,240
it's a little act of defiance

59
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:04,720
toward life.

60
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:06,620
There you are.